# Dynamic Type, Text Size, and Layout Switching

Found multiple relevant mentions:

## Dynamic Layout Switching to Vertical

**From the Contacts App Example:**
> "When the text size increases, the layout dynamically switches to a vertical stack allowing each cell to take the entire width of the display."

## Cells Taking Full Width

**From the Figure Example:**
> "Great. Now, when the text size changes to an accessibility size, the layout dynamically changes to provide more width to the text which makes it easy to read while avoiding truncations."

## Code Example: Dynamic Layout in SwiftUI

```swift
struct FigureContentView: View {
    @Environment(\.dynamicTypeSize) 
    private var dynamicTypeSize: DynamicTypeSize

    var dynamicLayout: AnyLayout {
        dynamicTypeSize.isAccessibilitySize ?
        AnyLayout(VStackLayout(alignment: .leading)) : AnyLayout(HStackLayout(alignment: .top))
    }

    var body: some View {
        dynamicLayout {
            FigureCell(systemImageName: "figure.stand", imageTitle: "Standing Figure")
            FigureCell(systemImageName: "figure.wave", imageTitle: "Waving Figure")
            FigureCell(systemImageName: "figure.walk", imageTitle: "Walking Figure")
            FigureCell(systemImageName: "figure.roll", imageTitle: "Rolling Figure")
        }
    }
}
```

This demonstrates switching from `HStackLayout` (default) to `VStackLayout` (accessibility sizes) to allow cells to use full width.
